as night fell on valentine's day they  gathered in small groups in various  parts of russia  the aim to show solidarity with  opposition leader alexei navalny who's  currently in jail  in playgrounds and courtyards they place  candles in the shape of a heart  and shone lights from mobile phones the  coordinated action came in response to a  call from a man called leonid volkov  now based in lithuania he's a close ally  of alexey navalny  he wants russians to copy tactics used  by pro-democracy activists in  neighboring belarus  our force is that we are  more sophisticated than them that we are  more  creative and we have to think about  other forms of protest  and he already invented something volkov  urged people to post pictures of  sunday's gatherings on social media  using the slogan love is stronger than  fear the aim was to avoid large  demonstrations  of the type that's seen thousands of  people arrested across russia  in recent weeks among them alexei  navalny's wife who's now reportedly in  germany  and his spokesperson kira yarmish they  were among the women activists being  honoured in the second city saint  petersburg  around 100 women formed a human chain  near a monument to victims of political  repression  i think it will have an impact at least  we'll show the world that we're here  that those people are not alone that we  stand in solidarity with them  navalny was arrested in january  immediately after flying back to moscow  he'd spent many months in germany  recovering after he was poisoned with a  nerve agent  an attack that nearly killed him on  friday he was in court  facing slander charges which he's  dismissed as politically motivated  he's already been sentenced to nearly  three years in jail for parole  violations  while he was convalescing abroad after  the recent crackdown his team postponed  mass rallies until at least the spring  and just a few days ago president putin  suggested the street protests were not  really about navalny  you know what this person under  investigation  is being used precisely at the moment  when in countries all over the world  including our own people are tired  irritated and discontented  about the conditions in which they live  and their income  but if the authorities continue to go  after political activists  this type of event could well gain  momentum nadine barber al jazeera
 

